From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Henrik Klee <henrik@goat-code.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 21:02:48 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] Bluetooth: hci_bcm: Add iPad Air 2 BCM4350C2

Match the iPad Air 2's BCM4350C2 with the plain hci_bcm sequence: the
patchram loaded at 115,200 baud, with no early baud change. On a J81
that sequence started the controller (Riesling USI STC patchram, build
1529) and found classic and LE devices in a scan. The iPad 5 and iPad 7
Apple board sequence has not been tried on this chip.

Assisted-by: LLM
---
 drivers/bluetooth/hci_bcm.c | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/bluetooth/hci_bcm.c b/drivers/bluetooth/hci_bcm.c
index d1634b2bc54a..ecf32c2c7192 100644
--- a/drivers/bluetooth/hci_bcm.c
+++ b/drivers/bluetooth/hci_bcm.c
@@ -1688,6 +1688,8 @@ static const struct of_device_id bcm_bluetooth_of_match[] = {
 	/* The iPad 5 BCM4355C0 needs the same sequence as the iPad 7 C1. */
 	{ .compatible = "apple,j71t-bcm4355c0-bt",
 	  .data = &bcm4355_j172_device_data },
+	/* The iPad Air 2 BCM4350C2 runs the plain sequence at 115,200 baud. */
+	{ .compatible = "apple,j81-bcm4350c2-bt" },
 	{ .compatible = "apple,j71b-bcm4355c1-bt",
 	  .data = &bcm4355_j71b_device_data },
 	{ .compatible = "apple,j172-bcm4355c1-bt",
